     "kind": "logistics",
     "blocks": "finding the last cases, where the last cases are",
     "what": "The remaining burden sits in the Democratic Republic of the Congo and in pockets of the Central African Republic, South Sudan, Angola and Guinea — which is to say in the places least reachable by a mobile screening team. This is the last-mile problem in its literal form: active case-finding requires travelling to villages with no roads, in areas with active conflict, to test people who feel well. And the arithmetic worsens as the programme succeeds. Screening ten thousand people to find one case costs the same as screening ten thousand to find fifty, so cost per case found rises steeply exactly when the political case for spending is weakest. A single-dose oral treatment would change this more than any logistics investment, because it would collapse screen-confirm-stage-treat into one visit.",
