     "units": "fraction alive — **and this is one of the few natural histories in medicine that was measured properly**, from sanatorium-era cohorts before chemotherapy. Roughly 70% of smear-positive tuberculosis is fatal within ten years; smear-negative disease kills about 20%. The rest self-cure or become chronically infectious, which is why the untreated figure is not near zero",
