    "witness": "**The largest untreated-to-treated gap in the register from a drug alone**, and it is seventy years old. Streptomycin's 1948 trial is the origin of the randomised controlled trial as an institution, so this row is simultaneously the register's biggest single therapeutic gain and the methodological event that made the rest of the column measurable. **The gap between 0.90 and the actual global figure is not biology.** It is diagnosis, adherence support and drug supply — this record's `access` axis — which is why tuberculosis still kills over a million people a year with a curative regimen that costs a few tens of dollars."
