     "blocks": "completing six months of therapy, and thereby not manufacturing resistance",
     "what": "The paradigm case for this blocker kind, and the only one in the register where non-adherence does not merely fail the patient but PRODUCES A WORSE PATHOGEN for everybody else. Six months of daily multi-drug therapy, begun when the patient often already feels better after two, in populations facing displacement, informal work, stigma and cost. Partial treatment selects for resistance; the MDR stratum in this record is what that looks like at scale. This is why regimen shortening is not a convenience feature. Cutting six months to four, or resistant treatment from two years to six months, is an adherence intervention delivered as pharmacology, and it acts on transmission and resistance as well as on the individual.",
