     "what": "One vaccine in a century, and it does not do the job that matters. The binding constraint is that nobody knows what protective immunity looks like, so there is no correlate of protection and therefore no way to screen candidates short of running a full efficacy trial in a high-burden population — which is slow, enormous and expensive, and only a handful of such trials can run at once. This is the one genuinely scientific blocker in the record. Everything else here is delivery. `scale: null` because a correlate of protection cannot be bought; the trials that follow it can.",
