     "toll": "major",
     "what": "Many lesions, heavy bacillary load, weak cell-mediated response — the lepromatous end of the spectrum. Twelve months of therapy, and a substantially higher rate of leprosy reactions both during and after it. Those reactions are treated with prolonged corticosteroids, and in recurrent erythema nodosum leprosum with thalidomide, whose own history is inseparable from this disease. THE SPECTRUM IS A PROPERTY OF THE PATIENT, NOT THE ORGANISM. The same bacterium produces tuberculoid disease in a person with strong cell-mediated immunity and lepromatous disease in a person without. That is unusual enough to be worth stating: this record's strata partition by HOST RESPONSE rather than by pathogen, stage or geography, which is a fourth kind of partition and the schema is indifferent to which."
