     "why": "WHO recommended multidrug therapy, replacing dapsone monotherapy. Dapsone alone took years, generated widespread resistance and left many patients on indefinite treatment; MDT cures in six to twelve months with rare relapse. A genuine capability change rather than a toll reduction, and the second the register has recorded on the intervention axis after hepatitis C's direct-acting antivirals.",
