    "Why new case detection has been flat at around 200,000 a year for two decades. Whether that is a stable transmission equilibrium or a stable detection capacity is the question, and the two imply opposite responses.",
    "What triggers leprosy reactions, and who will have one. This is where the disability comes from and nothing predicts it.",
