     "kind": "logistics",
     "blocks": "self-care and rehabilitation for three to four million disabled people",
     "what": "The single largest deliverable in this record, and it is not a drug programme. Most leprosy disability is progressive rather than fixed: insensate hands and feet are injured because they cannot be felt, and the ulcer-injury-resorption cycle is stopped by daily inspection, protective footwear, wound care and splinting. Reconstructive surgery restores function in some. None of that is what MDT delivery is built for, and the people who need it have by definition finished treatment and left the register. This is exactly the lymphatic filariasis shape — tablets are donated and organised and the intervention for the disabled population is soap, shoes and training — and it is the second record to show that the residue is the treatable part (gaps.md #60).",
