     "units": "estimated infections/year, chiefly the south-western United States, northern Mexico and parts of Central and South America — **against roughly twenty thousand reported annually in the United States.** The order-of- magnitude gap is not uncertainty about the organism; it is that most infection is mild or silent and most symptomatic disease is diagnosed as bacterial pneumonia and never tested for",
