     "what": "**UNIFORMLY FATAL BEFORE AZOLES, AND NEVER CURED SINCE.** Fluconazole controls it; stopping it relapses roughly four patients in five, so therapy is lifelong. Hydrocephalus is common and frequently needs a permanent shunt; strokes from basilar vasculitis, and permanent neurological deficit, are not rare. **The one stratum in this record where the answer is `suppressive`, and the reason the entity spans the ladder.** It has no MONDO term of its own, checked the day this record was written."
