    "what": "**The toll is mostly paid by people who did not need the treatment**, which is a shape the register has recorded for cancer screening and not for an infection. Azoles are given for months to years: fluconazole and itraconazole cause hepatotoxicity, alopecia, dry skin and cheilitis, and interact widely; **fluconazole is teratogenic at the doses used here**, which matters because pregnancy is itself a major risk factor for dissemination. Amphotericin B, for severe disease, brings its usual nephrotoxicity. Rated `permanent: false` because these reverse on stopping. **The permanent prices — the shunt, the stroke, the cavity — belong to the disease and are carried in `residue`.**",
