    "what": "**A shunt, a stroke, or a hole in the lung.** Meningeal disease leaves hydrocephalus needing permanent shunting, and basilar vasculitis causes strokes with lasting neurological deficit. Pulmonary disease leaves cavities that can bleed or rupture, and fibrosis that permanently reduces lung function. Bone and joint disease leaves destroyed joints. **And there is a residue this schema cannot hold at all: the disease is over and the therapy is not.** A person with controlled coccidioidal meningitis is cured of nothing, has no active infection anyone can measure, and takes fluconazole for the rest of their life.",
