     "toll": "major",
     "what": "Retained placenta is managed by removing it. **Placenta accreta spectrum — where the placenta has grown into or through the uterine wall — is the stratum medicine manufactured.** It occurs at the site of a previous caesarean scar, its incidence has risen several-fold in step with rising caesarean rates, and it produces catastrophic haemorrhage usually managed by planned hysterectomy. **The commonest major operation in the world is generating a lethal complication of the next pregnancy** (gaps.md #147)."
