     "what": "Disseminated intravascular coagulation from abruption, amniotic fluid embolism, sepsis or the dilutional coagulopathy of massive transfusion itself. **This stratum cannot be treated without blood components** — fibrinogen, cryoprecipitate, platelets — and is therefore the one where the register's zero-sum constraint bites hardest (gaps.md #128)."
