     "what": "Ten to fifteen mites on an entire body, and an itch out of all proportion to that — because the itch is a delayed hypersensitivity reaction to mite products rather than to the burrowing itself. First infestation is silent for four to six weeks while sensitisation develops; reinfestation itches within days. Topical permethrin or a course of oral ivermectin clears it. The commonest reason treatment fails is that the household was not treated at the same time."
