     "toll": "major",
     "what": "THE SAME MITE, MILLIONS OF THEM. In people whose cell-mediated immunity is impaired — elderly, immunosuppressed, some neurological and developmental conditions — the mite proliferates without check, producing thick hyperkeratotic crusts teeming with organisms. It often does not itch, which is part of why it is missed. TWO CONSEQUENCES THAT THE SCHEMA CANNOT CARRY. First, these patients are **hyperinfectious** — a single case seeds outbreaks through a care home or a household, so two percent of patients drive transmission for the other ninety-eight (gaps.md #82). Second, crusted scabies is routinely misdiagnosed as eczema or psoriasis and treated with topical corticosteroids, which suppress what little immune response was containing the mite and make it dramatically worse."
