     "from": 0.25,
     "to": 0.45,
     "why": "**A MILLION FEWER CHILDREN A YEAR, AND IT IS ONE OF THE LEAST-DISCUSSED ACHIEVEMENTS IN THIS REGISTER.** Under-five pneumonia deaths fell from roughly 1.7 million in 2000 to roughly 700,000. Four things did it and none alone would have: **Hib conjugate vaccine**, which removed a leading bacterial cause almost entirely wherever it was introduced; **pneumococcal conjugate vaccine**, delivered through Gavi and an advance market commitment designed specifically to get a high-income-market vaccine into low-income countries quickly; **wider community access to oral amoxicillin** through integrated community case management; and **falling household air pollution** as solid-fuel cooking declined. Compare the malaria entry two records ago — same period, same funders, comparable lives saved, and one of them is a global cause with a public profile while the other is a line in a UNICEF report.",
