     "blocks": "two billion people cooking over a fire indoors",
     "obstacles": [],
     "what": "Household air pollution from solid-fuel cooking is a major risk factor for childhood pneumonia, and around two billion people still cook that way. Clean cooking is prevention, it is not administered by anybody in health, and it belongs to energy and finance ministries. **It also prevents four other records in this register** — chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, ischaemic heart disease, stroke and lung cancer — which is gaps.md #87's problem exactly: a single non-specific intervention whose benefit is spread across entities that are each rated separately, so no record can justify its cost and the register cannot sum it. Clean cookstove programmes have a long history of disappointing trial results, mostly because adoption is partial and households keep the old stove. Rated `documented` on the risk association and the policy failure, not on any claim that a particular stove programme works.",
