     "toll": "minor",
     "what": "**A tenth of the episodes and a wildly disproportionate share of the deaths, and the only stratum where the register cannot claim a cure.** It occurs in malnourished children, it makes them more malnourished, and **Cryptosporidium** is a leading cause with **no useful drug** — nitazoxanide, the only licensed agent, performs poorly in exactly the malnourished and immunocompromised children who get it. Rehydration keeps the child alive through an episode and does not end it. This stratum is the diarrhoea-malnutrition cycle made visible, and it is why the record flags ⧉."
