    "> **`access: 0.45` is the ORS coverage figure and it is doing duty as an access number when it is largely an adherence and belief number.** Supply is genuinely not the constraint in most of the shortfall, which makes this the record where `access` most clearly conflates *could not get it* with *did not use it*.",
    "> The residue figure attributes a share of global stunting to enteric infection. The association is strong and the causal fraction is genuinely contested between diarrhoea, diet, EED and everything else correlated with poverty. It is the largest and least defensible number in the file.",
    "> Strata fractions are reasoned from the pathogen studies and shift by age, season and setting; the persistent-diarrhoea share in particular is a small fraction of episodes and a large fraction of deaths, and the record's record-level scalars average that away (gaps.md #151).",
    "> All-ages deaths and under-five deaths are both quoted and the file rates against a mixture, with the strata and interventions written mostly for children. Adult and elderly diarrhoeal death — a real and rising share in ageing populations — is barely represented.",
