     "to": 0.35,
     "why": "**A MOLECULAR CLASSIFICATION THAT CHANGED WHO GETS TREATED, IN BOTH DIRECTIONS.** The Cancer Genome Atlas sorted endometrial cancer into four groups — POLE-ultramutated, mismatch-repair-deficient, p53-abnormal, and no specific molecular profile — and it entered the WHO classification and the guidelines. **POLE-mutated tumours do so well that trials now test giving them no adjuvant treatment at all**, and p53-abnormal tumours are escalated. Same operation, same drugs, different people receiving them. Sentinel lymph node biopsy replacing full pelvic lymphadenectomy belongs to the same arc and removed a large amount of permanent lymphoedema. The numbers above are the toll's *incidence* rather than its severity, which `moved` cannot distinguish — fifth record to hit that limitation after breast, prostate, gastric and bladder cancer (gaps.md #26)."
