     "what": "**The stratum where iron does not work, and since 2001 we know exactly why.** Inflammation raises hepcidin, hepcidin degrades ferroportin, and iron is locked inside macrophages and enterocytes where the marrow cannot reach it — so oral iron is absorbed poorly and does not correct the anaemia. Includes the anaemia of `chronic-kidney-disease`, of cancer, of `rheumatoid-arthritis`, of chronic infection. **Erythropoiesis-stimulating agents and the HIF prolyl-hydroxylase inhibitors treat it and carry cardiovascular risk**, and the real treatment is the underlying disease, which is another record."
