     "toll": "major",
     "what": "Not curable, and the honesty of that word matters: metastatic breast cancer is treated indefinitely, through successive lines, until it stops responding. Median survival is measured in years and is far longer for HER2-positive disease than it was twenty years ago, with a small tail of very long survivors. But nobody is cured, and calling breast cancer a \"curable cancer\" without a stratum for these patients is the specific inaccuracy this block exists to prevent."
