    "witness": "**THE LARGEST SURVIVAL SHIFT IN ADVANCED SOLID-TUMOUR ONCOLOGY, AND THIS RECORD'S HEADLINE FIGURE HIDES IT.** 0.94 is dominated by early excisions that were always curable. The change that matters — half of metastatic patients now alive at five years where almost none were — is invisible in the average. Another instance of gaps.md's ⧉ problem, and an argument that `strata` should carry survival too."
