     "toll": "major",
     "what": "**THE STRATUM THAT CHANGED, AND THE ONE THE SCHEMA CANNOT RATE.** Five-year survival around half, against under a tenth before 2011. The survival curve flattens, and a proportion remain progression-free years after stopping treatment — which looks like cure and cannot yet be called one. Recorded as `suppressive` rather than `curative` on the conservative reading, and the choice is arbitrary in a way the register should be uncomfortable about. See gaps.md #118. BRAF V600 mutant disease, about half of cutaneous melanoma, has targeted therapy as an alternative or a sequence — faster responses, less durable."
