     "blocks": "an intravenous drug that much of the world cannot buy",
     "what": "**ECHINOCANDINS ARE FIRST-LINE EVERYWHERE AND AVAILABLE IN A MINORITY OF THE WORLD.** They are intravenous only, priced well above fluconazole, and absent from many national formularies — so a large share of global candidaemia is treated with fluconazole against *C. glabrata* and *C. krusei*, which are respectively frequently and intrinsically resistant to it. The prescriber is not making a mistake; the alternative is not in the building. **This is `cryptococcal-meningitis`'s flucytosine blocker in a different drug class**, and the second time in four fungal records that the binding constraint is a registered, affordable supply of a medicine that already exists. Rezafungin, a once-weekly echinocandin, changes the administration problem and not the price one.",
