     "what": "The largest single cause, and the one where the gap between best and typical care is widest — survival at 28 weeks exceeds 95% in a well-equipped unit and is close to zero in a health post. **The interventions that carry most of the achievable gain are not intensive care**: warmth, kangaroo mother care, support with feeding, bubble CPAP, and antenatal steroids given to the right mother. This stratum also carries the record's whole `toll`."
