     "what": "Sepsis, pneumonia, meningitis and — still, where immunisation has not reached — tetanus. **This stratum is where the `cre` record does its killing.** Carbapenem-resistant *Klebsiella* in South Asian and sub-Saharan neonatal units is, on that record's own reading, probably the centre of mass of the global CRE burden, in babies whose infection is never cultured and never counted. Chlorhexidine cord care, clean birth practice and maternal group B streptococcal prophylaxis are the cheap end."
