     "obstacles": [],
     "what": "**GESTATIONAL AGE IS THE MOST IMPORTANT NUMBER IN THIS RECORD AND A LARGE FRACTION OF THE WORLD'S PREGNANCIES DO NOT HAVE ONE.** It decides whether antenatal steroids help or harm, what a birthweight means, what to expect, and what to attempt. Establishing it requires an ultrasound before about 22 weeks; without one it is estimated from a remembered last menstrual period or from the baby's appearance after birth, both of which carry errors of weeks. Portable and AI-assisted ultrasound aimed at exactly this is one of the more promising things in global health and is not deployed at scale. The second half is neonatal sepsis. **A blood culture from a newborn requires a volume of blood that is a meaningful fraction of their circulation**, yield is poor, and the answer arrives after the antibiotic decision. So babies are treated empirically, in units where — per the `cre` record — the organisms are increasingly carbapenem-resistant, and nobody finds out what was actually there. **The invisible epidemiology and the wrong treatment have the same cause**, which is the sentence that record already wrote.",
