     "what": "**Nine in ten, and it is as close to a solved clinical problem as this register contains.** Fifteen minutes, day case, sutureless, an implanted lens, and the patient sees. Manual small-incision surgery achieves comparable outcomes without a phacoemulsification machine, faster and far cheaper, which is what makes high-volume programmes in low-income settings possible at all."
