     "what": "**THE STRATUM FIFTY YEARS OF TRIALS DID NOT REACH.** Leukaemia in the first year of life, almost always carrying a *KMT2A* rearrangement, arising from a lesion that occurred **in utero** — the initiating event is prenatal and is sometimes demonstrable on the newborn blood spot. Survival is under half and has moved little. Adding blinatumomab to infant protocols is the first substantial improvement in decades. Every other stratum here is a success story; this one is a frontier, and it is three percent of the record."
