     "obstacles": [],
     "what": "**THE PATIENT WHO WILL DIE CAN BE NAMED AT DIAGNOSIS AND NOTHING CAN BE DONE WITH THE NAME.** What BAP1 loss does to confer metastatic competence, why the liver, and what holds micrometastases dormant for a decade are all open — and the answer to any of them is the adjuvant therapy that every trial so far has failed to find. Downstream of that, the known driver pathway has been drugged and the survival curve did not move. Tebentafusp shows the immune route can be forced open in a low-mutation tumour; extending that beyond one HLA allele, and from months to years, is the open engineering half of the same question. `scale: null`.",
