     "what": "Plaque brachytherapy needs a radiation source, a physicist and an ophthalmic surgeon trained to place it; proton beam needs a proton facility. Both are concentrated in a small number of ocular oncology centres, almost all in high-income countries. Elsewhere the treatment is enucleation — survival-equivalent, so this blocker moves `toll` and not `efficacy`, and the register has no place to put a blocker on a toll. For a disease this rare, regional referral centres rather than national ones are the plausible answer, and the volume to sustain them is thin.",
