    "permanent": true,
    "what": "**THE OPERATION THAT CURES KIDNEY CANCER CAUSES KIDNEY DISEASE, AND CHRONIC KIDNEY DISEASE IS A QUEUED RECORD IN THIS REGISTER.** Radical nephrectomy removes a whole kidney and roughly halves nephron mass in a patient who frequently has hypertension and diabetes already. The resulting reduction in filtration is permanent, raises cardiovascular risk, and in some patients progresses. **Partial nephrectomy exists precisely to avoid this** and is technically harder, and its adoption has been slower and more uneven than the evidence warrants. **TYROSINE KINASE INHIBITORS ARE TAKEN INDEFINITELY AND FELT DAILY.** Hypertension, hand-foot skin reaction, fatigue, diarrhoea, mucositis, hypothyroidism. Individually manageable and collectively the reason many patients reduce or stop, in a disease where the drug works while you take it. **CHECKPOINT BLOCKADE** adds immune-related adverse events, and the endocrine ones — thyroiditis, hypophysitis, occasionally type 1 diabetes — are permanent hormone replacement in exchange for a response. **AND HIGH-DOSE INTERLEUKIN-2 DESERVES RECORDING BECAUSE IT WAS ABANDONED.** For two decades it was the only therapy that produced durable complete remissions in metastatic RCC, in perhaps one patient in fifteen, at the cost of capillary leak, vasopressors and intensive care for everyone who received it. Checkpoint inhibitors replaced it, and **an enormous toll disappeared from this record without capability changing** (gaps.md #26, #138).",
