     "why": "**ANTI-ANGIOGENIC THERAPY, AND RENAL CELL CARCINOMA IS WHERE IT ACTUALLY DELIVERED.** Sunitinib and sorafenib replaced interferon and high-dose interleukin-2 as standard treatment for metastatic disease, roughly doubling median survival. It followed directly from the mechanism: clear cell RCC loses *VHL*, stabilises HIF, and overproduces VEGF, so it is among the most vascular tumours there is. **A pathway worked out from a hereditary syndrome produced a drug class for the sporadic disease** — and anti-angiogenesis, which underdelivered in most cancers, worked here for exactly that reason."
