     "to": 0.58,
     "why": "**CONCURRENT CHEMORADIATION, AND IT IS THE MOVE THAT MADE THIS A CURABLE DISEASE RATHER THAN A RADIOSENSITIVE ONE.** Intergroup 0099 randomised radiotherapy alone against radiotherapy with concurrent cisplatin followed by adjuvant chemotherapy in advanced nasopharyngeal carcinoma, and the survival difference was large enough that the trial was stopped early. Concurrent chemoradiation has been the backbone ever since. **Worth noting what did not happen.** No new molecule was involved — cisplatin dates from the 1970s and radiotherapy from before that. What changed was **giving them at the same time instead of one after the other**, which is a scheduling result rather than a discovery, and it is the same shape as `asthma`'s 2019 guideline entry and `rheumatoid-arthritis`'s treat-to-target. The register keeps finding that a substantial share of progress is arrangement rather than invention.",
