     "why": "**THE ONLY WORKING BLOOD-BASED CANCER SCREENING TEST IN THIS REGISTER, AND THE SECOND `moved` ENTRY EVER WRITTEN ON THE `measurement` AXIS.** Circulating cell-free Epstein-Barr virus DNA, measured in more than 20,000 Hong Kong men, shifted the stage distribution from a historical 5-7% stage I to **47% stage I**, with three-year progression-free survival of 97% against 70%. The two-step protocol — repeat the test at four weeks — converted an unusably false-positive-prone assay into a usable one. **State the limitation with the result, because this record will be quoted.** The comparator was a historical cohort rather than a randomised unscreened arm, so a mortality benefit is not demonstrated. Stage shift is exactly what lead time and overdiagnosis also produce, and this register holds `prostate-cancer` and `thyroid-cancer` because that is not a theoretical concern. **Why it is on `measurement` and not `access`.** Nothing about the treatment changed. What changed is when the disease is found, and gaps.md #184 says `moved` has no convention for measurement while measurement is what changes most. `cerebral-palsy` wrote the first such entry; this is the second, and `check.py` still does not validate the axis.",
