     "why": "**INDUCTION CHEMOTHERAPY BEFORE CHEMORADIATION, AND THE EVIDENCE CAME ALMOST ENTIRELY FROM THE COUNTRIES WHERE THE DISEASE IS.** Adding gemcitabine and cisplatin as induction before concurrent chemoradiation improved recurrence-free and overall survival in locally advanced disease. Alternative induction regimens reported similar gains across the same period. **The authorship is the part worth recording.** These were Chinese trials, run in Chinese centres, on a disease concentrated in southern China, and they set the global standard of care. **It is the clearest counterexample in this corpus to the pattern where evidence is generated in high-income countries and exported** — here the endemic region generated it, and the rest of the world adopted it.",
