     "date": 2002,
     "axis": "toll",
     "from": "catastrophic",
     "to": "catastrophic",
     "why": "**A NON-MOVE ON THE AXIS AND A LARGE ONE IN PRACTICE.** Organ-preserving approaches — glansectomy, laser, topical therapy — and sentinel node biopsy in place of routine inguinal dissection became established through the 2000s, and centralisation into specialist networks spread them. **For a man treated early at a specialist centre the toll is now moderate rather than catastrophic.** The record-level rating does not move because it describes the modal patient globally, who presents late and is not treated at such a centre. Dated loosely.",
