     "what": "**The stratum that grew, and the one the diagnostics fit worst.** Severe influenza and COVID-19 both predispose to invasive pulmonary aspergillosis in patients who are not classically immunosuppressed; corticosteroid treatment for those illnesses compounds it. Galactomannan on serum performs poorly here, so diagnosis leans on bronchoalveolar lavage in patients too unstable for bronchoscopy. **COVID-associated pulmonary aspergillosis was being argued about while it was killing people**, which is what a diagnostic category with no reference standard produces."
