     "what": "**AZOLE-RESISTANT *ASPERGILLUS FUMIGATUS* IS SELECTED IN THE ENVIRONMENT BY AGRICULTURAL FUNGICIDES, AND ARRIVES IN AZOLE-NAIVE PATIENTS.** The resistance alleles most commonly found in patients — tandem repeats in the promoter of the *cyp51A* gene, with associated point mutations — are the same ones found in soil, compost, flower-bulb waste and plant debris, and they confer cross-resistance to the medical azoles. A person who has never taken an antifungal can inhale a resistant strain and present with a disease for which the only oral treatment does not work. **NO OTHER RECORD IN THIS REGISTER HAS THIS SHAPE.** `amr-infection` names bacteria and its levers are stewardship, infection control and new agents — all of which act inside the health system, in a loop that runs through prescribers and patients. **This loop contains neither.** The intervention is restricting or redesigning agricultural fungicides, and the actor is an agriculture ministry weighing crop yield against a clinical harm that lands on somebody else entirely. That is a policy problem with no clinical counterparty, and the register has no other instance of it.",
