     "what": "**THE FIELD FORMALLY DIAGNOSES BY LIKELIHOOD BECAUSE CERTAINTY IS UNOBTAINABLE.** \"Proven\", \"probable\" and \"possible\" are consensus categories, proven requires tissue, and the patients who most need biopsy are thrombocytopenic and hypoxic. Culture is insensitive; galactomannan works in neutropenic haematology and materially worse in the ICU, in solid-organ transplant and in anyone already on mould-active prophylaxis — which is much of the highest-risk population; CT signs are suggestive and neither sensitive nor specific. The consequences run in both directions and both are expensive. Patients who have it are treated late, and a much larger number who do not are treated empirically with a toxic, interacting, expensive drug **that also selects for the resistance in the blocker above.** A reliable non-invasive test would be worth more here than any new antifungal.",
