     "obstacles": [],
     "what": "**MOST HEAVY DRINKERS DO NOT GET CIRRHOSIS AND MOST FATTY LIVERS NEVER PROGRESS.** Genetic modifiers are established and replicated — PNPLA3, TM6SF2, and a protective HSD17B13 variant — and they account for a minority of the variance. The rest is not understood, and it matters practically: **it would identify who to watch and who to leave alone**, in populations numbering hundreds of millions. The second half is antifibrotic therapy. Fibrosis regression happens **spontaneously when the cause is removed** — stellate cells deactivate, collagen is degraded — and it happens slowly and incompletely, and past a threshold of vascular remodelling not at all. **No drug reliably accelerates it**, despite decades of targets, and every candidate class has failed in late-phase trials. A drug that made fibrosis regress on purpose would matter most in exactly the population that cannot remove the cause — the person who cannot stop drinking, the person whose metabolic disease will not shift — and it would convert the `residue` in this file from partly-permanent to treatable. `scale: null`.",
