     "to": 0.4,
     "why": "**BCG, AND WHAT IT CHANGED WAS WHETHER PEOPLE KEPT THEIR BLADDERS.** Before intravesical BCG, high-grade non-muscle-invasive disease and carcinoma in situ progressed often enough that early cystectomy was a reasonable answer. After it, most of those patients are managed with an intact bladder. Capability barely moved — these patients were curable by cystectomy before and are curable by cystectomy now. **What collapsed is the fraction who need it**, which is `toll.incidence` rather than severity, and `moved` records a change on an axis rather than in one of its components. Fourth record to hit that limitation after breast, prostate and gastric cancer (gaps.md #26). **And it is a live tuberculosis vaccine, adopted empirically, still not fully explained.**"
