     "why": "**ENFORTUMAB VEDOTIN WITH PEMBROLIZUMAB** replaced platinum chemotherapy as first-line treatment for advanced urothelial carcinoma, with a survival improvement large enough to change practice immediately — the biggest advance in metastatic disease since cisplatin combinations arrived in the 1980s. A five-point move at record level, because the stratum it reached is a tenth of diagnoses and the therapy is not curative. The same arithmetic as melanoma's and non-Hodgkin lymphoma's recent entries (gaps.md #61)."
