     "toll": "minor",
     "what": "**A different disease under the same name, and it is enormous.** Different organisms — group B *Streptococcus*, *E. coli* and *Klebsiella*, the last increasingly carbapenem-resistant — different presentation (a baby who is simply not right, with none of the adult criteria applicable), and a burden concentrated in South Asia and sub-Saharan Africa where the diagnostics do not exist. Survivors carry neurodevelopmental impairment at rates the adult literature would find alarming. It is the intersection of this record, `cre` and the queued `neonatal-conditions`, and all three under-describe it."
