     "toll": "major",
     "what": "**STAGE IV THAT IS SOMETIMES CURED**, which almost nothing else in this register can say. Liver-limited colorectal metastases resected, often after chemotherapy to shrink them, give long-term survival in a meaningful fraction. The register generally treats metastatic disease as a wall; here it is a door for a small group, and identifying that group is a surgical judgement rather than a biomarker."
