     "blocks": "antivenom (curative)",
     "what": "A textbook market failure. Sanofi discontinued Fav-Afrique, an effective pan-African antivenom, in 2014 — the stated reason was commercial, and no equivalent replaced it. Buyers are among the poorest rural populations on earth, so willingness-to-pay is near zero while manufacturing cost is not. WHO added snakebite envenoming to its neglected tropical diseases list in 2017 and set a target of halving death and disability by 2030.",
