     "date": 1997,
     "axis": "efficacy",
     "from": 0.35,
     "to": 0.5,
     "why": "**RITUXIMAB — THE FIRST THERAPEUTIC MONOCLONAL ANTIBODY APPROVED FOR ANY CANCER.** Adding an anti-CD20 antibody to CHOP chemotherapy improved survival in diffuse large B-cell lymphoma substantially, and the same addition helped across essentially every CD20-positive entity in the category. It is the founding case of antibody therapy in oncology in the way imatinib is the founding case of targeted small molecules, and it arrived four years earlier. **It reached only the B-cell side.** T-cell lymphomas have no CD20 and got nothing, which is why they are still the worst stratum in this record thirty years later.",
