     "blocks": "delivering a cell therapy that has to be manufactured per patient",
     "obstacles": [],
     "what": "CAR-T is not a drug that can be stocked. Cells are collected from the patient, shipped, engineered, expanded, shipped back and infused, over weeks during which aggressive lymphoma may progress beyond the point of benefit. Manufacturing slots are limited and manufacturing failures happen. The patient must be at a qualified centre for infusion and for a monitoring period afterwards. **The constraint is a supply chain with a human being inside it**, which is unlike anything else in this register — and it is why bispecific antibodies, which are off the shelf and give up some efficacy, matter more globally than the more effective product.",
