     "what": "**THE CAPABILITY `gonorrhoea` IS ASKING FOR EXISTS HERE AND IS UNEVENLY DEPLOYED.** Macrolide resistance is conferred by identifiable 23S rRNA mutations detectable from the same specimen that made the diagnosis. Resistance-guided therapy — sequential doxycycline then azithromycin or moxifloxacin according to genotype — raises cure from roughly forty percent to above ninety, and is standard in Australia and parts of Europe. **Most of the world has neither the organism test nor the resistance test.** A patient with persistent urethritis then receives sequential empirical antibiotic courses, which is precisely the behaviour that generated the resistance being worked around. This is an unusually clean purchasable intervention: **the assay exists, the drugs are generic, and the gain is a doubling of cure rate with no new science.** It is also the strongest available argument for the equivalent investment in `gonorrhoea`, where the same approach would let a defeated drug be used in the patients whose strain never lost it.",
