     "what": "Two questions, and the second would change how the whole register ranks this record. Whom to treat: anticysticidal drugs help many patients and endanger some, the danger is the inflammatory response to the parasite dying, and nothing predicts who will have a severe one. Guidance rests on lesion count, stage and location, which is a rule rather than a prediction. A marker would convert a judgement call into a decision. How much epilepsy: the commonly quoted figure is around a third of cases in endemic areas. If that is right, neurocysticercosis is among the largest preventable neurological burdens in the world, and a one-dollar dose given to asymptomatic carriers is one of the cheapest interventions against it. `scale: null` — the attributable-fraction work is fundable epidemiology and the predictive marker is not something that can be bought.",
