     "what": "**WHICH CIN2 WILL BECOME CANCER.** Roughly half regress in young women, and nobody can say which half. So they are excised, and the excision raises the risk of preterm birth in a later pregnancy. A marker that identified the regressing lesions would remove a real harm from a large number of young women without giving up any of the prevention — the same shape prostate cancer's active surveillance took, and here the beneficiary is a future child (gaps.md #117). **AND METASTATIC DISEASE HAS LITTLE.** Checkpoint blockade added an increment; there is no targeted therapy of consequence; and the stratum is a fifth of diagnoses because of late presentation rather than because of biology. `scale: null`.",
