     "what": "The chemotherapy backbone is generic. HER2 testing plus trastuzumab, mismatch-repair or PD-L1 testing plus checkpoint blockade, and claudin 18.2 testing plus its antibody are not — and they are the whole of what changed in advanced gastric cancer in the last fifteen years. **They reach about a tenth of the record**, which means a health system that can afford endoscopy, surgery and generic chemotherapy captures most of the available benefit and misses the part that is growing. Trastuzumab biosimilars have helped and the newer agents are on patent.",
