     "what": "Tetralogy of Fallot, transposition of the great arteries, atrioventricular septal defect, coarctation. **These required the invention of cardiopulmonary bypass and are now routine**, with survival to adulthood the expectation. Repaired is not the same as normal: residual lesions, scar-related arrhythmia, and **planned reoperation** — a repaired tetralogy usually needs a pulmonary valve in adult life."
