     "what": "**THE LARGEST STRATUM AND THE ONE THE REGISTER EXISTS TO NAME.** FOLFIRINOX or gemcitabine with nab-paclitaxel, in patients well enough to receive them, buying a median of months. Immunotherapy does not work. **KRAS is mutated in almost all of them and as of 26 August 2026 it is druggable** — daraxonrasib in the second line, hazard ratio 0.40 against chemotherapy, and nobody is cured. Most of what good care does for these patients is **biliary stenting, pain control including coeliac plexus block, enzyme replacement, nutritional support and hospice** — none of which alters the course, and all of which the register scores as nothing (gaps.md #98)."
