     "toll": "minor",
     "what": "Where the disease is genuinely solved, and where almost nobody is caught. Treated in the acute phase, in infancy, or in childhood, benznidazole cures at rates approaching those of any antimicrobial — and in congenital infection, treating the newborn works so well that screening pregnant women and treating their babies is one of the highest-yield programmes in the register. The acute phase is mostly asymptomatic or a brief fever, so it is almost never recognised outside an outbreak."
