     "what": "Destruction of the enteric nervous system leaves an oesophagus or colon that cannot propel. Management is dilatation, myotomy and resection — mechanical answers to a mechanical problem, as with the fibrosis in Crohn's. The nerves do not come back, and killing the parasite does not bring them back either."
