     "units": "deaths/year — **almost entirely neonatal herpes**, which is rare and severe: roughly fourteen thousand cases a year worldwide, with mortality concentrated in disseminated and central-nervous-system disease. Herpes simplex encephalitis in adults adds a smaller number. **Genital herpes itself kills essentially nobody**",
