    "note": "**Five hundred million people and four thousand deaths.** The burden of this record is neither mortality nor, for most people, physical illness: it is recurrent discomfort in a minority, a small number of catastrophically affected newborns, and — at a scale nothing here can measure — the psychological cost of a permanent diagnosis for a condition that is common, mild and heavily stigmatised."
