     "toll": "major",
     "what": "**CML'S OLD ENDING, AND THE ONE PLACE THE STORY DOES NOT HOLD.** Blast crisis behaves as an acute leukaemia, responds poorly to TKIs alone, and is treated with intensive chemotherapy plus a TKI and taken to allogeneic transplant if possible. It is now uncommon because patients are caught and treated in chronic phase — **the stratum shrank because the treatment worked**, which is a form of progress the register records nowhere."
