    "witness": "**THE FLAGSHIP TRANSITION IN THIS REGISTER: 0.0 TO 0.95, AND THE DATE IS 1922.** Nothing else here moves that far. It is also the cleanest demonstration of why `untreated` is the more interesting column — the treated figure says medicine is good at this, and only the untreated figure says what that is worth. **And the axis is silent about the rest of the record.** `ongoing: high`, a permanent daily burden, a toll this field cannot see. Surviving is not the same as being well, which is why `survival` is an addition to the register rather than a replacement for it."
