    "note": "**The prevalence and the harm are almost unrelated, which is why this record is hard to rate.** Two billion carriers, and the great majority will never have a symptom attributable to it. The disease is concentrated in three small populations: fetuses whose mothers are infected during pregnancy, people whose immunity fails, and the minority who develop retinal disease. Reading the prevalence as a burden figure would be the worst misreading available here."
