     "what": "**The leading infectious cause of posterior uveitis worldwide**, and it recurs — a retinal scar reactivates years or decades later, from the cysts at its edge. Treatment shortens an episode and does not prevent the next one. Lesions at the macula cost central vision permanently. Southern Brazil reports far higher rates and more aggressive disease, attributed to more virulent local strains."
