     "what": "Primary maternal infection in pregnancy, crossing the placenta. **Transmission risk rises through gestation and severity falls**, so early infection is rare and devastating while late infection is common and mild. Most infected newborns look normal and declare themselves later, chiefly with chorioretinitis. The severe form is hydrocephalus, intracranial calcification and chorioretinitis together. **The efficacy figure is the least secure in the record** and the reason this entity is treated as a screening question in some countries and ignored in others."
