     "what": "Reactivation disease generally, of which the cerebral form dominates. **Untreated toxoplasmic encephalitis in advanced HIV is fatal**, and it was among the defining opportunistic infections of the epidemic before antiretroviral therapy and co-trimoxazole prophylaxis. Induction therapy controls the acute episode; **maintenance must continue until immune reconstitution, because the cysts are still there** — which is the only stratum here that earns `suppressive`, and it earns it for the same reason the whole record cannot be cured."
