     "toll": "major",
     "what": "**THE MECHANISM HOLE, MADE COUNTABLE.** Neutrophilic, paucigranulocytic, obesity-associated and smoking-associated asthma responds poorly to corticosteroid and has no targeted therapy — every biologic on the market aims at the type-2 pathway these patients do not have. Tezepelumab, which acts further upstream at the epithelium, helps some of them and is the only thing that does. **This stratum is why the record rates `mechanism: partial` rather than `established`**, and it is the four percent that carries a disproportionate share of the maintenance-steroid toll."
