     "blocks": "an interpretable literature, and therefore any trial that settles anything",
     "what": "The same incommensurability that afflicts ME/CFS, arrived at by the opposite route, and the contrast is the useful part. In ME/CFS there is no biomarker, so no two groups can be sure they enrolled the same patients. HERE THERE IS A BIOMARKER AND THE PROBLEM PERSISTS, because one camp requires it and the other does not. A trial conducted under consensus-2 criteria is not interpretable to a consensus-1 clinician, and a trial under consensus-1 enrols a population the consensus-2 camp regards as a small unrepresentative subset. Two literatures, one name, and no way to pool them. This is what makes the definitional dispute a delivery problem rather than an academic one: it is not that the evidence is thin, it is that the evidence cannot be added up.",
