     "blocks": "what ends wound healing, and what fails to end it here",
     "what": "**WOUND HEALING HAS A TERMINATION STEP AND NOBODY KNOWS WHAT IT IS.** The normal sequence resolves: fibroblasts undergo apoptosis, the matrix remodels, the scar flattens and matures. In a keloid the building phase continues for years and spreads into skin that was never wounded. The literature describes what the persisting tissue is made of and what pathways are elevated in it; it does not describe the signal whose absence allows it. **THAT IS WHY EVERY TREATMENT IS DESTRUCTIVE OR SUPPRESSIVE.** Steroid, 5-fluorouracil, cryotherapy and radiotherapy all reduce the population of cells doing the building. **None of them delivers the stop signal, because nobody knows what it is**, and the tendency survives all of them — which is why the lesion returns and why the next wound does the same thing. Tagged `growth-control` (FND-O-0015), and this is the corpus's only record that sits on both of that obstacle's faces simultaneously: it is the repair programme, and it will not stop. **If the obstacle's unifying claim is right anywhere, it is right here**; if keloid turns out to be unrelated to the mechanism that limits organ size, the obstacle should split. `scale: null`.",
