     "blocks": "there is no animal that does this",
     "what": "**KELOIDS ARE NOT KNOWN TO OCCUR SPONTANEOUSLY IN ANY SPECIES BUT OURS.** No mouse, no rat, no pig, no primate model reproduces the defining feature — invasion beyond the original wound margin with no regression. The substitutes are implanted human keloid tissue in immunodeficient mice, which studies the lesion detached from the immune system that may be producing it, and cultured keloid fibroblasts, which studies the cells detached from everything. **So there is no system in which to test a drug against the thing that actually defines the disease**, and the field has proceeded by trying agents borrowed from oncology and dermatology directly on patients. That is not a criticism of the field; it is what is available. A direct instance of `no-model-system` (FND-O-0013), and an unusual one — the register's other entries there concern organisms that will not grow outside a host. **This is a disease that exists only in humans**, which is the same wall reached from the opposite direction. `scale: null`.",
