     "toll": "major",
     "what": "**The stratum medicine solved, and the word for what it did is `suppressive`.** Relapses abolished, new lesions abolished, disability progression markedly slowed — indefinitely, on treatment, in a young person who would previously have been told to expect a wheelchair. **The proportion of people with MS using wheelchairs has fallen and time to needing a walking aid has lengthened substantially over three decades.** What it is not is a cure: stop the drug and activity returns, and disability still accrues silently underneath (see `witness.intervention`)."
