     "what": "THE BINDING CONSTRAINT ON THE THING THAT MATTERS, and it is an industrial problem rather than a scientific one. A pandemic strain would be sequenced within days. Conventional egg-based influenza vaccine manufacture then takes roughly six months to reach population scale, and the first wave of a respiratory pandemic does not take six months. Existing stockpiles are matched to clades selected years in advance and would probably not match. What would close it is surge capacity in platforms that can be reprogrammed from a sequence — which exists now in a way it did not in 2009, and is not licensed, built out or contracted for influenza at the scale required. **Third use of the `manufacturing` blocker kind in forty-seven records**, and by a wide margin the largest sum at stake.",
