     "blocks": "why the pressure is high in nine out of ten people",
     "obstacles": [],
     "what": "**\"ESSENTIAL\" HYPERTENSION MEANS HYPERTENSION WHOSE CAUSE IS UNKNOWN, AND IT IS 90-95% OF THE DISEASE.** Sodium handling, renin-angiotensin-aldosterone activity, sympathetic tone, arterial stiffness, endothelial function and obesity all contribute, none is sufficient, and the relative weight differs between people in ways nothing measures. Genome-wide association studies have identified over a thousand loci, explaining a modest fraction of variance and producing **no new drug target** — a useful caution for every record in this register that treats genetic discovery as a route to therapy. The practical cost is that treatment is empirical. A clinician picks a class, waits weeks, measures, and switches — because nothing predicts which mechanism is dominant in this patient. **Renin profiling would be the mechanistic answer and is not in routine use**, and the race-based prescribing recommendation that stands in for it is a proxy that most people involved agree is a poor one. A drug acting on a newly understood mechanism would matter far less here than in most records, because the existing drugs work and reach a quarter of patients. **This blocker is a scientific hole in a record whose problem is not scientific**, and stating that clearly is more useful than inflating it. `scale: null`.",
