     "efficacy": {
      "value": 0.5,
      "units": "fraction-of-stratum (acute illness shortened by early antiviral)",
      "src": "reasoning"
     },
     "toll": "minor",
     "what": "Reactivation from dorsal root ganglia, decades later, as cell-mediated immunity declines. Lifetime risk roughly one in three and rising steeply with age. **Ophthalmic zoster threatens sight; geniculate zoster — Ramsay Hunt — causes facial palsy and hearing loss; disseminated zoster in the immunosuppressed can kill.**"
