     "toll": "major",
     "what": "**ONE OF THE GREAT THERAPEUTIC ACHIEVEMENTS IN MEDICINE, AND ALMOST NOBODY RECEIVES IT.** Four drug classes — a renin-angiotensin blocker or sacubitril/valsartan, a beta-blocker, a mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist, and an SGLT2 inhibitor — each independently reduce mortality, and taken together they roughly halve it and add years of life. Devices add more: defibrillators prevent sudden death, resynchronisation improves function in a defined group. **Most of it is off patent.** Registry data consistently find only a small percentage of eligible patients on all classes at target dose (gaps.md #210)."
