     "what": "Retinitis, colitis, pneumonitis, and graft dysfunction. **This is where the drugs work** — ganciclovir, valganciclovir, foscarnet, cidofovir, and since 2017 letermovir for prophylaxis in stem-cell transplantation, which is effective and unusually free of the marrow and renal toxicity that characterises the rest. **CMV retinitis was a leading cause of blindness in AIDS and largely disappeared with antiretroviral therapy**, which belongs to `hiv`."
