     "what": "THE BINDING CONSTRAINT, AND IT IS NOT A SCIENTIFIC ONE. Candidate vaccines exist and have existed for years, including one built on **the same rVSV vector platform as the licensed Ebola vaccine** — a platform proven in humans, in an outbreak, against a virus in the same family. Candidate monoclonals exist and protect non-human primates. None is licensed, because the market is roughly ten cases a year in expectation, in the poorest places, and no revenue model survives contact with that arithmetic. Ebola escaped this only because 2014 was catastrophic enough to change what governments were prepared to fund, and the vaccine that saved it had itself been sitting unlicensed for about a decade. **Marburg has not had its catastrophe.** The register's own reading of that is uncomfortable: this record's rating is a bet that not enough people have died yet.",
