     "what": "The one thing that demonstrably works here is a drip, a laboratory, and staff who can correct electrolytes for a week — and the case fatality difference between outbreaks with that and outbreaks without it is the largest effect in this record. Marburg emerges in mines, in villages, and in places a long way from any of it. Delivering it means moving a treatment unit, a laboratory and trained people into a remote area within days, and then paying to keep that capability in existence during the years when there is no outbreak — the stockpile problem gaps.md #57 keeps finding from new directions. Cheap per patient. Impossible to justify per year.",
