     "kind": "knowledge",
     "blocks": "a drug that works in the children who die of this",
     "what": "**NITAZOXANIDE APPEARS TO REQUIRE THE IMMUNE RESPONSE ITS PATIENTS DO NOT HAVE.** It gives a modest benefit in immunocompetent people — who mostly recover regardless — and no established benefit in malnourished children or in advanced immunosuppression, which is essentially the whole mortality of this disease. **A treatment that works only in people who do not need it is a distinct failure mode**, and the register has no other clean example. Why is not established. The standard reading is that the drug is parasitostatic and leaves clearance to the host, so a host that cannot clear does not clear — inference from trial subgroups rather than demonstrated mechanism. Malnutrition and cryptosporidiosis also worsen each other, so the failing population is the one whose immunity the disease is itself degrading. `scale: null`.",
