     "what": "**CHLORINE DOES NOT KILL IT**, at the concentrations used in drinking water and swimming pools — so the single intervention that underpins safe water worldwide fails against this organism specifically. What works is filtration, ultraviolet or ozone treatment, protected catchments, and keeping livestock slurry out of source water. All are infrastructure, all are capital, and none belongs to a health ministry. **Milwaukee, 1993 is the demonstration**: a filtration failure in a chlorinated municipal supply, an estimated four hundred thousand people ill — the largest waterborne outbreak recorded in the United States, in a wealthy city with a working utility. Recreational water outbreaks recur annually for the same reason. Where the deaths actually are, the intervention is the same and larger: water and sanitation infrastructure, which is the most purchasable and least health-sector thing in this record.",
