     "blocks": "fibrosis, which does not reverse",
     "what": "**NOTHING REMOVES SCAR FROM A LUNG, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE OF WHY THIS DISEASE IS FATAL.** Collagen deposited in the alveolar interstitium is not remodelled away. Antifibrotics slow the rate at which more is laid down; **no agent has ever recovered lost lung function in this disease**, and none is close. That makes the ceiling on every treatment the amount of lung a patient still has when they start, which is why the `window` matters so much and why a diagnostic delay is a permanent subtraction. **This is `tissue-repair`'s sixth citing record and one of its clearest.** Cardiac scar, brain distal to an infarct, emphysematous alveoli, fibrosed bowel — and fibrotic lung. **The obstacle is the same in each: mammals replace functional tissue with scar and cannot reverse it**, and this record differs only in that the process is ongoing rather than the residue of a single event. **Two further holes underneath it.** The initiating injury is unidentified — the genetics name susceptibility, not trigger — and nobody has explained why the disease begins subpleurally and basally with such regularity. And **the acute exacerbation has no mechanism and no treatment**, while being the commonest way the disease kills. `scale: null`.",
