     "what": "A week of fever, myalgia and cough, and then it is over. Rest, fluids, antipyretics — and antivirals shorten it by about a day if they are started in time, which they usually are not. **Almost nobody in this stratum dies and almost all of the world's antiviral prescriptions are written for it.**"
