     "what": "Primary viral pneumonia, **secondary bacterial pneumonia** — classically *Staphylococcus aureus* or pneumococcus, and the mechanism by which the 1918 pandemic did most of its killing — decompensated heart failure, exacerbated COPD, and myocardial infarction in the week after infection. **Treatment here is oxygen, ventilation and antibiotics for the bacterial superinfection**, which is to say it is treatment of the consequences. Corticosteroids, which help in this exact clinical picture when the virus is SARS-CoV-2, are associated with worse outcomes here."
