     "toll": "minor",
     "what": "**HALF THE INFECTED POPULATION, AND THE STANDARD OF CARE IS DELIBERATE NON-TREATMENT WITH INDEFINITE MONITORING.** Low replication, normal transaminases, no significant fibrosis — the evidence that antivirals help them is genuinely weak, and the recommendation is six-monthly review for life. Rated `intervention: none` because that is literally what happens, and it is why this record flags ⧉. **Two things make it uncomfortable.** Monitoring for life requires an infrastructure that mostly does not exist, so in practice these patients are told they have a virus that may kill them, given no treatment, and lost to follow-up. And WHO's 2024 guidelines **expanded eligibility substantially**, moving people out of this stratum — which means its size is a judgement that has already moved once and is partly a rationing decision (gaps.md #162)."
