     "kind": "policy",
     "blocks": "anybody mobilising for the people who are already infected",
     "obstacles": [],
     "what": "**THE VACCINE SOLVED THE FUTURE AND THE PRESENT WAS LEFT WHERE IT WAS.** Two hundred and fifty-four million people are chronically infected, almost all of them infected before the vaccine reached them, and about 3% are on a thirty-dollar-a-year generic that would prevent a large share of their deaths. New chronic infections have collapsed. **Both facts are true and only one of them gets attention.** **`hiv` is the control case and it is decisive.** Same shape of disease — chronic virus, no cure, lifelong suppression, cheap generics, stigma — and it reaches 0.72 in this register against this record's 0.08. HIV was not easier. HIV got a global emergency framing, dedicated financing at the scale of PEPFAR and the Global Fund, sustained patient activism, price negotiation as a public campaign, and named international targets that governments were measured against. **Hepatitis B got a vaccine and was filed as handled.** `chagas` is the second instance and is worse: vector control succeeded, roughly six million infected people remain, over ninety percent were never diagnosed, and its reach in this register is 0.03. **A prevention that works makes the prevalent cohort invisible, because funding follows incidence and the stock is not incidence** (gaps.md #163). Rated `documented`: the coverage figures, the financing asymmetry and the target architecture are all matters of public record. It is not a claim that anybody obstructed anything.",
