    "witness": "**THIS IS THE RECORD THAT SHOWS WHAT `survival` CANNOT SEE.** The band reads `a chance`, which puts ALS beside `pancreatic-cancer`. But pancreatic cancer's 13% are *cured* — they are alive at five years and the disease is gone. **ALS's 20% are alive at five years and still dying of it.** Nobody in this record is cured, ever, and the difference between those two columns is the difference between the axis being useful and being misleading (gaps.md #216). **And the gain from 0.15 to 0.20 is mostly not a drug.** Riluzole adds two to three months of median survival. Non-invasive ventilation adds considerably more, and attendance at a multidisciplinary clinic is associated with longer survival than any medication in this record. **The survival curve moved because of a machine and a clinic**, which is a sentence this register keeps writing and which the pharmacology-shaped view of progress keeps missing."
