    "permanent": false,
    "what": "**ALMOST NOTHING IN THIS RECORD IS DONE TO THE PATIENT BY MEDICINE, AND THAT IS ITSELF THE FINDING.** Riluzole requires liver monitoring and is otherwise well tolerated. Edaravone is an infusion or an oral suspension. Tofersen is an intrathecal injection every four weeks. Gastrostomy and non-invasive ventilation are interventions with ordinary procedural risks. **None of it disfigures, disables or permanently costs the patient anything**, and the register's `toll` machinery — built for facial nerves, laryngectomies and myeloablation — has very little to record. **The one genuinely heavy decision is tracheostomy ventilation**, which can extend life by years in a body that continues to fail around it, and which is chosen by a small minority in most countries and a much larger one in Japan. That is not a toll in this schema's sense; **it is a choice about how to die, offered by technology and answered differently by different cultures**, and no field here holds it. **Everything that is taken from a person with ALS is taken by the disease.** The register records what treatment costs and has no column for that.",
