     "what": "**DOZENS OF PHASE 3 TRIALS HAVE FAILED AND THE FIELD DOES NOT AGREE ON WHY.** Three explanations compete and they have different consequences. **The compounds did not work** — the simplest and probably true for most. **The model was wrong**: the SOD1 mouse became the standard preclinical gate for all ALS, including the 98% of patients without SOD1 mutations, and it predicted a long series of human failures. **Or the trials enrolled a mixture**: if ALS is several diseases converging on one syndrome, an unstratified trial dilutes any real effect toward the null. **The methodological consequences are being acted on** — platform trials with shared placebo arms, enrichment by progression rate, biomarker-based endpoints — and it is too early to say whether they help. **And there is a specific tension this record should state.** Patient advocacy in ALS is unusually effective and has secured approvals on thin evidence, of which AMX0035 is the clearest case: approved in 2022, phase 3 negative, withdrawn in 2024. **That sequence is the system working**, and it is also two years of patients taking something that did not work instead of joining a trial. The register records both halves and adjudicates neither. **Tagged `animal-translation` (2026-08-30).** This blocker is the sharpest statement of that obstacle in the corpus and the reason it was written: a faithful model of 2% of the disease became the entry requirement for all of it, and a decade of candidates passed through it into negative trials.",
