    "witness": "**`terminal` BY THE BAND AND BY EVERY OTHER READING.** Six percent at five years, and unlike `als` a small number of those people are genuinely long-term survivors rather than slowly dying — which makes this record the *other* side of gaps.md #216. **ALS at 0.20 is entirely delay; glioblastoma at 0.06 is mostly delay with a real tail of something closer to cure.** One axis, three meanings, and the field still cannot tell them apart. **The number has moved and it is worth being precise about how much.** Before 2005, median survival on radiotherapy alone was around twelve months; adding temozolomide took it to about fifteen and roughly doubled two-year survival. That is a real gain and it is two and a half months of median life, in a disease that has absorbed four decades of the best-funded cancer research there is."
