     "from": 0.12,
     "to": 0.2,
     "why": "**THE STUPP PROTOCOL, AND THE FACT ABOUT IT THAT MATTERS IS THE DATE.** Adding temozolomide to radiotherapy after surgery increased median survival from about 12.1 to 14.6 months and roughly doubled survival at two years. It became the standard of care immediately and **it is still the standard of care twenty-one years later.** **No cancer in this register has gone longer without its standard being displaced.** Compare `melanoma`, transformed twice since 2011; `non-hodgkin-lymphoma`, twice since 1997; `cml`, once and completely. Dozens of phase 3 trials in glioblastoma have failed in the intervening period — anti-angiogenics that improved progression-free survival and not overall survival, checkpoint inhibitors that did nothing, vaccines, oncolytic viruses, targeted agents against EGFR. **Two and a half months of median survival is the whole of what four decades of the best-funded cancer research has bought this disease**, and stating that plainly is more useful than the alternative.",
