     "why": "**TUMOUR TREATING FIELDS, AND IT IS THE MOST CONTESTED ENTRY IN THIS RECORD.** Alternating electric fields delivered through scalp electrodes worn continuously; a randomised trial reported a median survival gain of several months when added to temozolomide. It is approved and used, and **it is not accepted everywhere** — the trial was open-label with no sham device, the mechanism is debated, the device must be worn most of the day with a shaved scalp, and several national bodies have declined to fund it. **Record the disagreement rather than adjudicating it.** A treatment that cannot be blinded, in a disease with no alternatives and a desperate population, is exactly the situation in which the evidence is hardest to read and the pressure to accept it is highest. `witness.contested` carries the argument.",
