     "axis": "mechanism",
     "from": "none",
     "to": "established",
     "why": "**THE PAPER THAT NAMED THE CAUSE, AND IT CAME FROM A MINING DISTRICT.** Wagner and colleagues described a series of mesothelioma cases in the asbestos-mining region of the North Western Cape in South Africa, linking the tumour to crocidolite exposure — including in people who had never worked in the mines but lived near them. **That last detail is why this entry matters as much as it does.** Domestic and environmental exposure counted, not only occupational, which established that the hazard was not confined to the workforce and made the case for banning the material rather than protecting the workers. **And then it took forty years.** The United Kingdom banned all asbestos in 1999, the European Union in 2005. **The interval between knowing and stopping is the finding**, and it is longer than the latency of the disease.",
