     "blocks": "a rare cancer that cannot power the trials it needs",
     "what": "**THIRTY THOUSAND CASES A YEAR, SCATTERED ACROSS EVERY COUNTRY THAT EVER USED ASBESTOS, AND TWO PRACTICE-CHANGING TRIALS IN TWENTY YEARS.** Pemetrexed in 2003 and combined checkpoint blockade in 2020. Between them, almost nothing succeeded, and the surgical question took two randomised trials across two decades to answer in the negative. **The trial problem is structural.** The disease is uncommon, the population is elderly with occupational lung disease, survival is short enough that accrual competes with attrition, and the histological subtypes behave differently enough that stratification splits an already small sample. **It is `marburg`'s problem with the numbers changed** — not too few patients in one place, but too few anywhere. **The consequence is that mainstream practice ran ahead of evidence for decades and had to be walked back.** Radical surgery was standard in specialist centres, believed in, and offered to patients, and it took until 2024 to establish that it should not be. **That is the system correcting itself and it is also thousands of major operations that should not have happened.** **What would change it is what has changed it elsewhere**: international platform trials with shared control arms, which for a disease this rare is not an efficiency but the only way to ask a question at all. **Tagged `validation-throughput` (2026-09-02), and this record is the floor face of that obstacle rather than the volume one.** Everywhere else the complaint is that there are more candidates than capacity to test them. Here the gate is not too narrow — **it is too wide.** The minimum viable trial is larger than the disease, and no budget changes that, because the constraint is how many people have the illness rather than how much anyone is willing to spend on them. What follows is the reason this record keeps arriving at single-arm studies against historical controls, which is the evidentiary standard four withdrawn drugs in this register are a warning about. **The obstacle's two faces want opposite things from a regulator and this record is one of them.**",
