     "value": 3e-06,
     "units": "new cases per person per year, dominated by children aged roughly five to ten — on the order of 300-400 a year in the United States and perhaps a few thousand worldwide. A reasoned estimate. **It is a small number and it is roughly a tenth of all paediatric brain tumours**, which are the leading cause of cancer death in children",
