     "to": "RT-QuIC on cerebrospinal fluid",
     "why": "**AN ASSAY BUILT OUT OF THE PATHOGENIC MECHANISM ITSELF.** Dated to the multicentre diagnostic-accuracy study rather than to the first description — the register's `moved` dates follow the evidence, because that is what the citation can support. Real-time quaking-induced conversion exploits the property that defines the agent: misfolded prion protein templates the conversion of normal recombinant protein, and the resulting aggregation is detected by fluorescence. Applied to cerebrospinal fluid it achieves high sensitivity and very high specificity, and it moved diagnosis from a clinical judgement supported by EEG, MRI and a non-specific surrogate marker to a laboratory test. **What it does not do is change any outcome**, and the record should say so. There is no treatment, so an earlier and more certain diagnosis buys certainty, the end of an often long and distressing diagnostic process, the ability to plan, access to trials, and accurate surveillance. **Those are real goods and none of them is survival**, which is why this is a `measurement` entry (gaps.md #184) and moves no other axis.",
