     "blocks": "an agent that survives the autoclave, and a reservoir nobody has sized",
     "what": "**THIS IS THE ONLY PATHOGEN IN THIS REGISTER THAT STANDARD STERILISATION DOES NOT DESTROY.** Prions resist conventional autoclaving, formaldehyde and alcohol. Decontamination requires extended autoclaving with sodium hydroxide or sodium hypochlorite, or single-use instruments — which means every neurosurgical, ophthalmic or neuroendoscopic procedure on an unsuspected case is a potential transmission event. **Several hundred iatrogenic cases arose exactly this way**, alongside cadaveric growth hormone and dura mater grafts, before the practices were changed. **And the reservoir is unsized.** Retrospective appendix surveys found abnormal prion protein in roughly one specimen in two thousand. If those people are incubating variant CJD, the subclinical population is orders of magnitude larger than the clinical one; if the finding is not disease, it is nothing. **Thirty years after the epidemic, nobody knows**, and the policy consequences — blood donor deferral, surgical instrument protocols, plasma-derived product sourcing — have been maintained on that uncertainty at real and continuing cost. **Recorded as `policy` rather than `knowledge` because the decisions are being made now, repeatedly, under uncertainty that may never resolve** — which is the shape `h5n1` records for preparedness and is here about a hazard already introduced rather than one anticipated.",
